1
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,020
Look with your heart and see

2
00:00:33,020 --> 00:00:36,000
Find the truth right here

3
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:39,000
Hey you good or bad, truth or lies

4
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:42,000
You can't escape this soul's gray smoke

5
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:45,000
Take all your courage

6
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:48,159
And maybe you'll save the world

7
00:00:48,159 --> 00:00:50,340
Mojo Mojo Mojo Spy

8
00:00:50,340 --> 00:00:53,760
Mojo Mojo Mojo Spy

9
00:00:53,760 --> 00:00:56,719
Mojo Mojo Mojo Spy

10
00:00:56,719 --> 00:00:57,939
Mojo Spy

11
00:00:57,939 --> 00:00:58,939
Mr. K betrayed the Illumin-Eye

12
00:00:58,939 --> 00:00:59,939
Hunted to a dead end, he fled by jumping into the river

13
00:00:59,939 --> 00:01:00,939
On the beach, Jingjing found the unconscious Mr. K

14
00:01:00,939 --> 00:01:01,939
Mr. K begged Jingjing to take him to the police station

15
00:01:01,939 --> 00:01:02,939
At the police station, Mr. K was interrogated

16
00:01:02,939 --> 00:01:03,939
He spills the secret that Dorothy wants to steal the ancient sword, the Eternal Flame

17
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:35,859
Ancient Sword Showdown

18
00:01:35,859 --> 00:01:43,280
I'm sorry

19
00:01:43,280 --> 00:01:45,599
I don't think that's necessary at all

20
00:01:45,599 --> 00:01:49,359
Chief

21
00:01:49,359 --> 00:01:50,099
You can rest assured

22
00:01:50,099 --> 00:01:52,640
We're fully prepared this time

23
00:01:52,640 --> 00:01:54,579
The theft of the Angel's Tear gem last time

24
00:01:54,579 --> 00:01:56,879
Has made me completely lose faith in you

25
00:01:56,879 --> 00:01:59,780
This time we'll guarantee it

26
00:01:59,780 --> 00:02:00,959
The safety of the artifacts in the museum

27
00:02:00,959 --> 00:02:04,659
We've already installed it in the venue.

28
00:02:04,659 --> 00:02:06,159
A more advanced security system.

29
00:02:06,159 --> 00:02:08,979
You should all go back and get some rest.

30
00:02:08,979 --> 00:02:09,680
See our guests out.

31
00:02:09,680 --> 00:02:12,759
Please

32
00:02:12,759 --> 00:02:18,159
Darn it!

33
00:02:18,159 --> 00:02:20,120
They actually look down on us!

34
00:02:26,879 --> 00:02:37,319
We went by the list Mr. K provided.

35
00:02:37,319 --> 00:02:40,299
The suspects from the Illumin-Eye organization have been arrested.

36
00:02:40,299 --> 00:02:43,060
Over 90% of the people on the list

37
00:02:43,060 --> 00:02:44,620
They're all people we suspected before.

38
00:02:44,620 --> 00:02:46,960
In the end, they all confessed.

39
00:02:46,960 --> 00:02:48,819
Was once involved with the Illumin-Eye organization.

40
00:02:48,819 --> 00:02:50,699
But the Illumin-Eye's lair...

41
00:02:50,699 --> 00:02:51,979
But there was no one left.

42
00:02:51,979 --> 00:02:54,659
If Mr. K's defection is real

43
00:02:54,659 --> 00:02:58,500
Then the Illumin-Eye abandons its nest.

44
00:02:58,500 --> 00:03:00,020
That's perfectly reasonable too.

45
00:03:00,020 --> 00:03:02,400
Jimmy

46
00:03:02,400 --> 00:03:04,099
What's the situation at the museum?

47
00:03:04,099 --> 00:03:06,780
Not going well.

48
00:03:06,780 --> 00:03:08,740
Because of the Angel's Tear thing.

49
00:03:08,740 --> 00:03:10,939
The museum director won't agree, no matter what.

50
00:03:10,939 --> 00:03:13,039
Hand the Eternal Flame over to us for safekeeping.

51
00:03:13,039 --> 00:03:17,419
I've already sent Inspector Sima and the others

52
00:03:17,419 --> 00:03:19,099
to stake out across from the museum.

53
00:03:22,819 --> 00:03:23,599
There he is.

54
00:03:23,599 --> 00:03:24,500
What?

55
00:03:24,500 --> 00:03:27,740
It's a...

56
00:03:27,740 --> 00:03:29,479
...flea of a guy.

57
00:03:29,479 --> 00:03:30,699
He's lurking around the museum.

58
00:03:30,699 --> 00:03:32,439
Snooping around—highly suspicious.

59
00:03:32,439 --> 00:03:39,419
Why the long faces?

60
00:03:39,419 --> 00:03:41,360
Mr.K said Flea is a psychic.

61
00:03:41,360 --> 00:03:42,580
And he's also

62
00:03:42,580 --> 00:03:43,400
one of Dorothy's men.

63
00:03:43,400 --> 00:03:46,520
Jimmy,

64
00:03:46,520 --> 00:03:47,599
put the museum

65
00:03:47,599 --> 00:03:48,620
under close surveillance now.

66
00:03:48,620 --> 00:03:50,120
Go.

67
00:03:50,120 --> 00:03:54,080
I'll send more plainclothes officers outside the museum.

68
00:03:54,080 --> 00:03:55,240
Arrest the suspect the moment he appears.

69
00:03:58,440 --> 00:03:59,200
Wait for me!

70
00:04:54,079 --> 00:05:12,079
Quick!

71
00:05:12,079 --> 00:05:13,459
Squad one, seal the back door.

72
00:05:13,459 --> 00:05:17,319
The rest of you, follow me.

73
00:05:17,319 --> 00:05:17,759
Go!

74
00:05:24,079 --> 00:05:29,459
So? How about it?

75
00:05:29,459 --> 00:05:32,459
Not bad, huh? My museum's security system?

76
00:05:32,459 --> 00:05:35,259
No matter how many robbers or thieves come, they'll all be caught.

77
00:05:35,259 --> 00:05:37,560
Comparing our security system to the police,

78
00:05:37,560 --> 00:05:39,279
which one works better?

79
00:05:39,279 --> 00:05:44,199
Forget it.

80
00:05:44,199 --> 00:05:45,159
They don't need us here.

81
00:05:45,159 --> 00:05:45,639
Let's go.

82
00:05:54,079 --> 00:05:58,399
Look at this.

83
00:05:58,399 --> 00:06:00,680
Here.

84
00:06:00,680 --> 00:06:00,899
Hello?

85
00:06:00,899 --> 00:06:02,500
Reporting, Captain Han.

86
00:06:02,500 --> 00:06:04,180
We've caught Flea.

87
00:06:04,180 --> 00:06:06,979
We're escorting him back to the station now.

88
00:06:06,979 --> 00:06:08,019
Nice work.

89
00:06:08,019 --> 00:06:09,339
Everything going smoothly?

90
00:06:09,339 --> 00:06:11,299
Why the hesitation?

91
00:06:11,299 --> 00:06:14,539
Actually, Flea

92
00:06:14,539 --> 00:06:16,180
was caught by the museum's

93
00:06:16,180 --> 00:06:16,939
security system.

94
00:06:16,939 --> 00:06:18,759
We just

95
00:06:18,759 --> 00:06:20,180
picked him up.

96
00:06:22,459 --> 00:06:23,560
We never even made a move.

97
00:06:23,560 --> 00:06:25,639
Flea had already been caught by the security system.

98
00:06:25,639 --> 00:06:28,939
Well, as long as the Eternal Flame is safe,

99
00:06:28,939 --> 00:06:31,899
what does it matter who caught the criminal?

100
00:06:31,899 --> 00:06:33,780
Forget it.

101
00:06:33,780 --> 00:06:34,540
Inspector Sima

102
00:06:34,540 --> 00:06:36,079
Bring the suspect back first.

103
00:06:36,079 --> 00:06:36,420
Then

104
00:06:36,420 --> 00:06:37,100
Wait

105
00:06:37,100 --> 00:06:39,340
Inspector Sima, did you only catch a flea?

106
00:06:39,340 --> 00:06:42,759
Yeah

107
00:06:42,759 --> 00:06:43,600
Strange

108
00:06:43,600 --> 00:06:47,420
Would the Illumin-Eye fail so easily? Huh

109
00:06:47,420 --> 00:06:49,879
Inspector Sima

110
00:06:49,879 --> 00:06:51,800
Did you find any trace of Dorothy at the scene?

111
00:06:51,800 --> 00:06:53,060
No

112
00:06:53,060 --> 00:06:54,920
What about Shaker?

113
00:06:54,920 --> 00:06:57,139
No trace either.

114
00:06:57,139 --> 00:06:58,740
Only found the flea.

115
00:06:58,740 --> 00:07:00,560
Quick, ask the flea.

116
00:07:00,560 --> 00:07:01,939
Where is Dorothy?

117
00:07:01,939 --> 00:07:04,519
Where is Dorothy?

118
00:07:04,519 --> 00:07:05,259
Talk now.

119
00:07:05,259 --> 00:07:08,420
Hmph, nothing to hide anyway.

120
00:07:08,420 --> 00:07:10,379
This time I acted alone.

121
00:07:10,379 --> 00:07:12,139
Damn it.

122
00:07:12,139 --> 00:07:13,699
Get back to the museum now.

123
00:07:13,699 --> 00:07:14,660
We fell into a trap.

124
00:07:14,660 --> 00:07:14,879
What?

125
00:07:14,879 --> 00:07:16,199
It's a trap.

126
00:07:16,199 --> 00:07:17,579
Inspector Sima

127
00:07:17,579 --> 00:07:19,459
Dorothy's creating a diversion

128
00:07:19,459 --> 00:07:20,500
Hurry back to the museum

129
00:07:20,500 --> 00:07:23,500
Turn around, quick!

130
00:07:23,500 --> 00:07:32,120
Jimmy

131
00:07:32,120 --> 00:07:34,319
What on earth is going on?

132
00:07:34,319 --> 00:07:37,120
The flea was just bait

133
00:07:37,120 --> 00:07:40,000
Dorothy played us

134
00:07:40,000 --> 00:07:42,620
I hope I'm wrong

135
00:07:42,620 --> 00:07:44,579
Let's wait to hear from Inspector Sima

136
00:07:50,500 --> 00:07:58,620
Those cops are actually guarding the entrance again

137
00:07:58,620 --> 00:08:01,500
I really don't know what those fools are worried about

138
00:08:01,500 --> 00:08:02,500
Hey~

139
00:08:20,500 --> 00:08:24,439
Ah, damn it!

140
00:08:24,439 --> 00:08:38,259
What the heck is going on here?

141
00:08:38,259 --> 00:08:40,220
Why are all the lights on in the middle of the night?

142
00:08:40,220 --> 00:08:42,379
Huh? Where is everyone?

143
00:08:42,379 --> 00:08:44,000
Where did everyone go?

144
00:09:06,000 --> 00:09:07,480
Someone must have broken in

145
00:09:07,480 --> 00:09:09,259
Quick, break down the door!

146
00:09:20,000 --> 00:09:21,299
Something big has happened!

147
00:09:25,299 --> 00:09:27,740
We screwed up again this time...

148
00:09:27,740 --> 00:09:28,740
Ending theme

149
00:09:33,860 --> 00:09:36,799
Nothing like

150
00:09:36,799 --> 00:09:41,000
the loneliness of being alone

151
00:09:41,000 --> 00:09:44,460
In those days of life

152
00:09:44,460 --> 00:09:48,919
There's bound to be some unhappiness

153
00:09:48,919 --> 00:09:52,059
Saying goodbye to today

154
00:09:52,059 --> 00:09:56,440
Always leaves us feeling lost

155
00:09:56,440 --> 00:09:59,860
Look toward tomorrow

156
00:09:59,860 --> 00:10:04,179
It waves to me on the horizon

157
00:10:04,179 --> 00:10:07,919
Each day is just the sun's rise and fall

158
00:10:07,919 --> 00:10:11,919
Turning into time, dreaming even more

159
00:10:11,919 --> 00:10:17,199
Awaiting every second of life

160
00:10:17,199 --> 00:10:23,679
Bright eyes are sparkling

161
00:10:23,679 --> 00:10:27,039
A smile that meets the sun

162
00:10:27,039 --> 00:10:34,639
Bravely speak the little joy you keep inside your heart

163
00:10:34,639 --> 00:10:39,080
Music blows in the morning breeze

164
00:10:39,080 --> 00:10:42,439
Carrying away dreams of many years

165
00:10:42,439 --> 00:10:45,100
Over the little bridge

166
00:10:45,100 --> 00:10:47,659
At the crossing by Thousand Shores Station

167
00:10:47,659 --> 00:10:52,759
Over the little bridge

168
00:10:52,759 --> 00:10:55,319
At the crossing by Thousand Shores Station